WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.147 --> 00:00:01.080
(gentle music)

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.430
- [Newscaster] These satellite images

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.440
show an ammunition depot

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.190
in the Russian-occupied parts
of Ukraine's Kherson region

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:12.150
in May and in mid-June 2023.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.890
This attack is one of a number

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.950
of Ukrainian strikes on
Russian military infrastructure

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.419
and supply lines in recent weeks.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.580
(gun firing)

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.120
As Ukraine continues the
push to take back territory,

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.270
Kyiv has been using
British long-range missiles

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.940
in an attempt to degrade Russia's ability

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.760
to defend the areas it occupies.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.710
Here's a closer look at the strategy

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.091
and the role of Western weapons.

00:00:37.091 --> 00:00:40.140
(suspenseful music)

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.170
In late June, Ukrainian
missiles struck a bridge

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.690
linking the occupied Crimean Peninsula

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.840
to the Russian-controlled
parts of the Kherson region,

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.033
Russian and occupation officials said.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.670
This bridge played a key role

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.680
in supplying Russia's frontline troops

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.053
in the south of Ukraine via Crimea.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.010
British intelligence said
the route's temporary closure

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.570
doubled the length of time it took

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.830
for Russian logistics convoys
to reach the front lines.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.200
The Russian-appointed
head of the Kherson region

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.513
dismissed the significance of the attack.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.910
Russian state media reported
that rocket fragments indicated

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.423
the bridge was hit with Storm
Shadow missiles from the UK.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.770
Ukraine's stepped up strikes
against infrastructure

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.870
deep in Russian-occupied territory,

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.640
came after London provided it

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.304
with long-range missiles in May.

00:01:32.304 --> 00:01:37.304
(Volodymyr Zelensky speaking
in foreign language)

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.510
- [Newscaster] The missiles
are fired from aircraft

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:46.200
and have a range exceeding 155 miles,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.972
enough to hit Russian
logistics hubs and bases.

00:01:49.972 --> 00:01:51.000
(missile blasting)

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.630
This is dramatically beyond
the reach of HIMARS launchers

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:56.820
sent by the US to Ukraine,

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.680
which were modified to keep their range

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.573
within about 50 miles.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.470
Last year, Kyiv
successfully used the tactic

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.710
of targeting Russian
supply lines with HIMARS

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.693
to retake the city of Kherson.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:13.620
However, Kherson was uniquely vulnerable

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.270
because Russian troops there

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:18.420
could only be resupplied over bridges.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.880
The Ukrainian and Russian
Ministries of Defense

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.310
didn't respond to a request for comments

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.220
on the significance of the
recent Ukrainian attacks

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.473
and the role of long-range missiles.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.990
Britain's Defense Secretary

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:34.650
speaking of the use of Storm
Shadow missiles in Ukraine,

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.180
urged Kyiv's Western allies

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.910
to provide more long-range equipments.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:40.830
- I think the key here
is to recognize that

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.450
if the Russians move out of range,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.220
we must work together, internationally,

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.900
to make sure that the equipment is given

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.060
to make sure they're back in range.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.970
- [Newscaster] In late June,
American and European officials

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.130
said the US was considering approving

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:56.130
a long-range missile system for Ukraine.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.280
In the meantime, these
attacks show Ukraine's focus

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.400
on destroying the support
system for Russian troops,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.593
while trying to preserve
troops and Western tanks.

00:03:05.593 --> 00:03:09.853
(gentle music)
(wind buffeting)

